 "audit_md": "## Data inspection (from `data/processed/mca_cutoffs_clean.json`)\n\n3,028 cut-off rows, years 2017\u20132026 (10 admission years; the brief assumed 8, the data has more, so there are more experiments).\n\n**Lists published per year** (R1 = first round, R2 = second round, SP = special rounds; 'result awaited' = separate lists for candidates whose degree result was pending):\n\n| Year | Round | Result-awaited list | Rows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2017 | R1 | no | 73 |\n| 2017 | SP1 | no | 27 |\n| 2017 | SP2 | no | 8 |\n| 2018 | R1 | no | 76 |\n| 2019 | R1 | no | 76 |\n| 2020 | R1 | no | 128 |\n| 2020 | R1 | yes | 144 |\n| 2021 | R1 | no | 208 |\n| 2021 | R1 | yes | 88 |\n| 2021 | R2 | no | 189 |\n| 2021 | R2 | yes | 50 |\n| 2022 | R1 | no | 256 |\n| 2022 | R2 | no | 205 |\n| 2023 | R1 | no | 234 |\n| 2023 | R2 | no | 216 |\n| 2024 | R1 | no | 151 |\n| 2025 | R1 | no | 270 |\n| 2025 | R2 | no | 352 |\n| 2026 | R1 | no | 132 |\n| 2026 | R2 | no | 145 |\n\n**Per year:**\n\n| Year | Rows | Colleges | Names without College ID | Female-seat rows | NCC/divyang rows | Converted rows | Domicile given | %-score rows | Rows used by benchmark |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2017 | 108 | 28 | 0 | 32 | 0 | 0 | 80 | 0 | 73 |\n| 2018 | 76 | 25 | 0 | 21 | 1 | 0 | 50 | 0 | 75 |\n| 2019 | 76 | 23 | 0 | 20 | 0 | 0 | 51 | 0 | 76 |\n| 2020 | 272 | 42 | 0 | 42 | 0 | 0 | 118 | 0 | 128 |\n| 2021 | 535 | 45 | 0 | 70 | 3 | 0 | 199 | 0 | 208 |\n| 2022 | 461 | 44 | 0 | 52 | 3 | 0 | 180 | 0 | 255 |\n| 2023 | 450 | 47 | 0 | 56 | 3 | 0 | 177 | 0 | 232 |\n| 2024 | 151 | 46 | 0 | 22 | 3 | 0 | 76 | 0 | 148 |\n| 2025 | 622 | 51 | 0 | 56 | 1 | 0 | 247 | 0 | 269 |\n| 2026 | 277 | 51 | 0 | 43 | 2 | 12 | 159 | 145 | 126 |\n\n**Columns and how often they are filled:** `college_id` 100%, `id_match` 100%, `institute_name_raw` 100%, `year` 100%, `round` 100%, `round_label` 100%, `result_awaited` 100%, `branch` 100%, `institute_type_raw` 96%, `fee_waiver_seat` 92%, `opening_rank` 100%, `closing_rank` 100%, `opening_score` 5%, `closing_score` 5%, `category_raw` 100%, `social` 100%, `seat_class` 77%, `gender` 100%, `after_conversion` 100%, `eligible_category_raw` 21%, `domicile` 44%, `domicile_raw` 44%, `total_allotted` 100%.\n\n**Quality checks:** exact duplicate rows: 0; 797 rows are printed splits of 272 seat pools (by domicile, or in 2025 by the candidate's own eligible category); they are not duplicates and are merged by taking the highest closing rank; missing closing rank: 0; missing opening rank: 0; opening rank > closing rank: 0. College-name \u2192 official ID matching (provisional = a college not in the current intake list, kept under its own ID): alias 163, exact 2692, provisional 173 rows.\n\n**What the data does and does not contain:**\n\n- Available every year: college, closing and opening **rank**, category (social/class/gender), seats allotted, round. Domicile is printed only in some years; it is merged, not compared.\n- **Graduation-percentage cut-offs** appear only in 2026 (145 rows). A percentage-based model therefore cannot be trained or tested across years.\n- **Individual allotments** (which student got which college) are not in the data: the merit lists that contain them hold personal data and are deliberately kept out. Allotment accuracy is therefore measured with simulated student ranks against the published cut-offs.\n- Round 2 lists exist for 2021, 2022, 2023, 2025, 2026 (none for 2024); special rounds only for 2017. Only Round 1 exists in every year, so the benchmark uses Round 1 to compare like with like.\n",
